op7t-0210: camera: CSIPHY1 and CSID in MIPI C-PHY mode (the IMX586 module is C-PHY)

0209 (2026-11-12): every arm stage passes (no freeze), the sensor streams
(frame_count 40), but the CSID sees nothing (RX/RDI0 IRQ status and byte
counters 0) and the buffer stays 0xa5. The decoded init table writes 0x0111
= 3: CSI signalling mode C-PHY. The 7T's main camera module runs MIPI C-PHY
with 3 trios (hence "3 lanes" in every mode); 0205 set the PHY up as D-PHY.

Now CSIPHY v1.1 (live DT qcom,csiphy-v1.1) as Qualcomm's downstream
cam_csiphy_core.c cam_csiphy_config_dev does 3-phase (OnePlus SM8150 kernel
source, cam_csiphy_1_1_hwreg.h csiphy_common_reg_1_1 / csiphy_3ph_v1_1_reg /
csiphy_irq_reg_1_1): lane enable 0x2a (bit 2i+1 per trio), 0x818/0x81c,
0x800 pulse, the 43 writes for each of trios 0..2 (settle 0x12), IRQ masks;
CSID RX CFG0 PHY type bit 24 = C-PHY. sweetcamdphy=1 keeps 0205's D-PHY.

Apply after 0209.
---
